# Demos are wiring

Three places, three jobs:

| Place | Owns |
|---|---|
| `src/<package>/` library | Relevant domain logic (hooks, HOCs, flatten, sessions, walks) |
| `src/demo-utils/` | Irrelevant-to-the-model work: **UI, styles, and other utils** that could live in an external kit |
| Package `demo/` | **Wiring only** — compose library + demo-utils, pass chrome/fixtures, seed Storybook |

Leave the ported [`src/drag-drop-tree/`](../../src/drag-drop-tree) **untouched** (library **and** `demo/`). Form DnD chrome stays in [`src/flat-dnd/demo/WebRecursiveEdit.tsx`](../../src/flat-dnd/demo/WebRecursiveEdit.tsx).

## What a demo may do

- Call library hooks / HOCs (`makeUseDialogs`, `useFlatListSession`,
  `useFollowUpAdd`, `followUpDraftsList`, …)
- Import widgets from `src/demo-utils/` and pass them as host chrome
- Seed Storybook `INITIAL_*` data

## What a demo must not do

- Own HTML, **`style={{…}}`**, or **layout knobs**. Package `demo/` is
  wiring only. Do not wrap the same markup in `Inline` / `Stack` /
  `Row` and pass `gap={8}`, `align="center"`, `fontSize={14}`,
  `margin`, `maxWidth`. Those numbers and tags live inside a **named
  widget**. The demo passes data and callbacks.
- Reimplement a library orchestrator (item/section sessions, `commitDraft`,
  extra-map walks, flatten/sync)
- Own HTML/styles that another demo also needs — that widget belongs in
  `src/demo-utils/`
- Invent flags that hide host composition (`embedded` instead of
  `sidebar: ReactNode | null`)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — layout primitive + leftover HTML; demo still owns the UI
<Inline gap={8} align="center">
  <strong>{section.header.title}</strong>
  {openSectionEdit && !section.header.deleted && (
    <button type="button" onClick={() => openSectionEdit(section)}>
      Edit
    </button>
  )}
</Inline>

// ✅ GOOD — widget owns markup, gap, and the Edit control
<HeadingEdit
  title={section.header.title}
  ready={openSectionEdit != null && !section.header.deleted}
  onClick={() => openSectionEdit(section)}
/>
```

A widget that **is** a specific control is named for that control and
bakes its label. Do not export a generic `QuietCheck` / `ToolbarCheck` /
`TextButton` that demos caption with `"Show deleted"`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — generic check; demo still owns the copy and the meaning
<QuietCheck checked={showDeleted} onChange={setShowDeleted}>
  Show deleted
</QuietCheck>

// ✅ GOOD — the widget is the control
<ShowDeleted checked={showDeleted} onChange={setShowDeleted} />
```

`Stack` / `Row` / `Inline` stay in `demo-utils` for **other widgets** to
compose. Package demos do not import them.

Heavy logic is either **extracted** (reusable, no HTML) or **removed** by
twisting the library so the demo can just wire it.

## `src/demo-utils/`

Generic widgets that could live in an external UI kit go here: page shell,
sidebar layout, confirm banner, dropdown **including the popover panel**,
phase tabs, JSON panels, editor dialog, labeled text field, field stack,
required mark, column picker, form title, review-status note, layout
(`Stack`, `Row`, `Inline`), list chrome (`FieldRow`, `SectionPanel`),
and every other visual. Package `demo/` must not contain `style={{…}}`.

Import only from `demo/` and `*.stories.tsx` — never from library `_deps` /
package source. Hosts pass the trigger, items, labels, and fixtures; they
do not restyle the panel. demo-utils must not import package `demo/` or
library types that a UI kit would not know.

One file per widget (`DemoPage.tsx`, `DropdownMenu.tsx`, …). `index.ts`
only re-exports. Do not dump components into `index.tsx`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — package demo owns popover chrome
<div style={{ position: "absolute", background: "#fff", boxShadow: … }}>
  {items}
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — DropdownMenu owns the panel
<DropdownMenu open={open} align="end" trigger={icon}>
  {items}
</DropdownMenu>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — shared field stack lives in a package helper
// form-edit/demo/editFormDemoHelper.tsx
export const FieldViewerChrome = ({ … }) => <div style={{ … }} />

// ✅ GOOD — UI kit widget; demos wire it
import { FieldViewerChrome } from "../../demo-utils";
```

Chrome **bags** (`sectionChrome`, `formChrome`) stay in package demos —
they are wiring: they pass demo-utils widgets into library render props.
Do not paste the same JSX into a second helper; import the widget.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — demo walks the tree and brands extras
const map = new Map();
const walk = (cols) => { … map.set(item.header.id, branded({…})) };

// ✅ GOOD — library walk; host brands at the leaf
extrasByItemId(sections, (item) => branded({ actions: itemActions(item) }))
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — boolean hides two host layouts
<FormDialogsEditor embedded={true} />

// ✅ GOOD — host names the empty chrome
<FormDialogsEditor sidebar={null} />
```

Related: `no-html-outside-demo.mdc`, `unify-demo-chrome.mdc`,
`no-zero-responsibility.mdc`.
